{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e1ebffbc1cb0eec51440bbe0ddd5c03ba6b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" /> are written in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d7104f34af16053b63ce7cfa87265d915c6105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> array of squares, one number in each square, in such a way that if two numbers are consecutive then they occupy squares that share an edge. The numbers in the four corners add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the number in the center?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97af68b0e27ddcc9bb656fba006759ed49696f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution by Mlux:\nDraw a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d7104f34af16053b63ce7cfa87265d915c6105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> matrix. Notice that no adjacent numbers could be in the corners since two consecutive numbers must share an edge. Now find 4 nonconsecutive numbers that add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Trying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f9e44d7f658fa5f994265939788f085f4587c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3+5+9 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" /> works. Place each odd number in the corner in a clockwise order. Then fill in the spaces. There has to be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in between the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  The final grid should similar to this.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262a82d366c81f043b7c12d5eac1ec87f190eaa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\newline 1, 2,  3\\newline 8,  7, 4\\newline 9,  6,  5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/7109c1cdb32ed1480317143a9aa4d78330171a84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"51\" height=\"30\" /> is in the middle.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we color the square like a chessboard, since the numbers alternate between even and odd, and there are five odd numbers and four even numbers, the odd numbers must be in the corners/center, while the even numbers must be on the edges.  Since the odd numbers add up to 25, and the numbers in the corners add up to 18, the number in the center must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/372c66f620a4b6ab2828843aee9242b84a3f2a05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 - 18 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"134\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that if a number other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in a corner, the two numbers adjacent to it must be the numbers before and after it. Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in an edge spot that isn't a corner, it will be adjacent to two corners, which isn't possible, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is not consecutive to two other numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can't go to an edge spot that isn't a corner. Therefore, two of the corner squares are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Filling in the table one by one, we can start with this WLOG:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/884d393bd659dd2be5f656cfa560934a7c670834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\newline 1, 2, \\_ \\newline \\_,  \\_, \\_ \\newline \\_,  \\_, \\_$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"65\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is not one of the answer choices, it cannot be in the center, so it must go in the corner adjacent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. That means the last corner is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6705162410742131f7cb5da64df0593f255104ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 - 1 - 3 - 9 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, we can keep filling in the table to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262a82d366c81f043b7c12d5eac1ec87f190eaa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\newline 1, 2,  3\\newline 8,  7, 4\\newline 9,  6,  5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>And our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/7109c1cdb32ed1480317143a9aa4d78330171a84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"51\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:StrikingTsunamiYT&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:StrikingTsunamiYT (page does not exist)\">StrikingTsunami</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_.28Problem_11-20.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fast Forward to 6:20 for problem 12\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o</a>\n</p><p>~THEMATHCANADIAN\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B\">2016 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235712\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 253/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1963/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5651/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.408      1 Template:AMC12_box\n100.00%    7.408      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14813:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235712 and revision id 275227. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}